{#
The toast after an action that can be undone: what happened, and an Undo.

One file because three actions end the same way — archive, a label change and
"Move to" — and the parts that must not drift between them are all here: which
controller the button is wired to, where it posts, and how long it stays.

Eight seconds rather than the usual four. A plain toast is read and dismissed;
this one has to be read, understood as a mistake, and reached with a pointer
that was on the other side of the screen. The token is single use and the
session holds only the last few (StatusUndoService), so the button going away
with the toast is the interface agreeing with what the server would say.

Variables:
  message    already translated
  undoToken  from StatusUndoService::remember()
#}
{% include '_partials/_toast.stream.html.twig' with {
    message: message,
    extra: {
        undo_url:        path('app_status_undo_run', { token: undoToken }),
        undo_controller: 'mail--status-undo',
        hide_after:      8000,
    },
} only %}
